## Robustness: does the order of the options matter?

Each of the 272 memory decisions was asked three times, with the options in three rotations (mention/quiet/skip, quiet/skip/mention, skip/mention/quiet).

| check | result |
|---|---|
| policy action changed with the order | 25/272 (9.2%) |
| decider's top label changed with the order | 8/272 (2.9%) |
| first-listed option picked as top label | 269/816 (33.0%); a bias-free model picks it as often as that option happens to be right |
| median / largest probability shift between orders | 0.03 / 0.19 |

Made by `eval/option_order.py`; answers saved in `eval/results/option_order.json`.

